From e747c3e3c437963a0a36600a535a3ebb5bb5cd3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harmonika AI <dev@harmonika.id>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:40:59 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] brand: single brand layer, env compat shim, upstream-free
 distribution

- packages/util/src/brand.ts is the only place product identity lives; config dir,
  config names, version/channel/artifact and URLs all read from it. env() resolves
  HARMONIKA_* first and falls back to OPENCODE_* so both names keep working.
- global.ts and config/discovery.ts consume Brand instead of literals; build.ts emits
  the CLI defines from Brand.
- upgrade no longer touches upstream: it reads the Harmonika manifest, verifies sha256
  and replaces the running binary (staged file on Windows). Package managers, brew,
  winget and the upstream release API are refused with guidance.
- updater service fails closed for every method, so nothing can silently install an
  upstream build; the TUI auto-check is opt-in via HARMONIKA_ENGINE_AUTOCHECK.
- pair --remote requires HARMONIKA_ALLOW_REMOTE_TUNNEL=1; stats prints harmonika.id.
